  "confidence": 0.62,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["T5", "R7", "T8", "R50", "T6", "T3"],
      "pins": ["T5.2", "T8.2", "R7.1", "R50.1", "R26.1", "R54.1"],
      "nets": ["NET0032", "NET0051", "NET0010", "NET0065"],
      "observed": "On the MAIN PUMP & VALVE DRIVERS sheet, the gate-limiting resistors are fed by the control nets (R26 100\u03a9 from NET0010 to the IRLR2905 T6 gate; R54 100\u03a9 from NET0065 to the AO3400A T3 gate), but the BT3904 level-shifter bases are fed by the float-switch input nets instead: R7 4k\u03a7 ties NET0032 to T5's base and R50 4k\u03a7 ties NET0051 to T8's base. NET0032/NET0051 are the FLOAT_LOW/FLOAT_HIGH nets (pulled up to +3V3 by R30/R25 in the WATER LEVEL SENSOR/SWITCHES block and routed to the ESP32 ADC/IO0/IO1 pins).",
      "expected": "Per the spec, the float switches are read as GPIO binary_sensor inputs, and the MOSFET gates are 'driven through R1 (100 \u03a9) from the ESP32 pin, pre-driven via T1/T4 (BT3904 NPN level shifter)' \u2014 i.e. the level-shifter base resistor must be on the same control net as the gate resistor (NET0010 for the main pump, NET0065 for the ATO valve), not on the float-input nets.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "R26 100\u03a9 \u2013 NET0010 \u2026 NET0005 (T6 gate); R7 4k7 \u2013 NET0032 \u2026 NET0008 (T5 base); R54 100\u03a9 \u2013 NET0065 \u2026 NET0076 (T3 gate); R50 4k7 \u2013 NET0051 \u2026 (T8 base) [MAIN PUMP & VALVE DRIVERS, sheet 1]"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "SW3/SW1 FLOAT \u2026 R30 10k / R25 10k to +3V3 \u2026 NET0051 / NET0032 [WATER LEVEL SENSOR/SWITCHES, sheet 1]"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "T2 \u2026 gate driven through R1 (100 \u03a9) from the ESP32 pin, pre-driven via T1 (BT3904 NPN level shifter) \u2026 Two float switches are read as binary_sensor GPIO inputs \u2026 matching \u2026 the netlist's FLOAT_LOW/FLOAT_HIGH nets"}
      ],
      "impact": "The main circulation pump and the ATO solenoid valve cannot be switched by their intended ESP32 control GPIOs (NET0010/NET0065 only reach the gates through the 100\u03a9 resistors). Their gate-drive level shifters are instead controlled by the float-switch inputs, which the firmware configures as high-impedance inputs with 10k pull-ups \u2014 far too weak to drive the transistor bases \u2014 so the pump/valve outputs become dependent on the float switches and the float-sensor readings are loaded/corrupted by the base currents. Dosing/ATO/circulation control does not behave as intended.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The power train, I2C pull-ups, buck/LDO feedback, TMC2209 current-sense and VREF networks, and the isolated/non-isolated sensor routing all match the spec, but the main-pump and ATO-valve gate-drive level shifters (T5/T8) are wired to the FLOAT_LOW/FLOAT_HIGH input nets (NET0032/NET0051) via R7/R50 instead of to the pump/valve control nets (NET0010/NET0065), a connectivity deviation that prevents correct GPIO control of the pump and valve."
}

